# First-run Tutorial

::summary
The gate screen. One screen, four choices, no way around it: until a user
finishes the tutorial every `/next` surface answers 303 back here (the
server-side gate in `next_surface` / `next_page_ctx`). There is deliberately NO
sidebar and NO topbar on this page — a gate that renders ten nav rows which all
bounce straight back to it is a lie about what the user can do. The only chrome
is the Surfy drawer the shell composes into every surface, which is where the
run itself happens once a lane is chosen.

Each choice is a real zero-JS `<form method="post">` (the email-triage MPA
idiom: no fields, the lane rides the action URL) posting to
`/tutorial/start`, which answers 303 back here with the drawer forced open
and the server-owned starter prompt + conversation id stamped on the shell root
as data attributes. No inline script, so no new CSP hash.
::

::app-shell[name=tutorial layout=sidebar-main-panel height=900]

:::tab-content[tab=main width=640 align=center]

# Welcome to Surfspace!

Ask Surfy to create:

::::form[submit="App" action="/tutorial/start?choice=app" method=post]
::::

::::form[submit="Doc" action="/tutorial/start?choice=doc" method=post]
::::

::::form[submit="Presentation" action="/tutorial/start?choice=presentation" method=post]
::::

::::form[submit="Tasks" action="/tutorial/start?choice=tasks" method=post]
::::

:::

::

Pick one and Surfy builds it with you. The artifact is created BEFORE the first
token streams (`tutorial::precreate_artifact`), so the run always ends with
something real to open even if the model says nothing useful. The turn is comped
server-side — derived from the conversation id the server minted, never from a
client flag.
